Chapter: ConstraintConcrete
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Inside a `Show a =>` function, `show` on a CONCRETE value must use
 normal dispatch, not the type-parameter's dictionary. Tests: literal
 args, let-bound concrete values, and the type-parameter arg.

Section: Types

  Color = | Red | Green | Blue  deriving Show

Section: Body

  describe : Show a => a -> Text
  describe (x) = show 5 & "/" & show x

  describe-let : Show a => a -> Text
  describe-let (x) = let n = 42 in show n & "/" & show x

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (describe Red)
    print-line-uni (describe Green)
    print-line-uni (describe-let Blue)
  end

